# gamescope — built FROM SOURCE via a novadeck-owned PKGBUILD (packages/gamescope/PKGBUILD),
# NOT fetched from the holo monorepo. build-overlay.sh sees `pkgbuild_local` below and uses that
# checked-in recipe instead of curl'ing one; makepkg still clones the upstream git source (the
# gamescope tag + its submodules) named in it.
#
# This switched from the holo `pkgbuild_repo` fetch (was pinned at holo's 3.16.17-1) to a local
# PKGBUILD bumped to gamescope 3.16.25. Reason: 3.16.17's Wayland explicit-sync
# (linux-drm-syncobj) WSI present path intermittently deadlocks on the first frame on this HW,
# wedging ~2/3 of cold session starts. We already rebuild gamescope from source for the
# composite-rotation patch, so we bump the version here (same medicine as packages/mesa) rather than
# carry a runtime workaround. See docs/bringup-phase2.md step 1e + the gamescope-flip-blocker
# memory, and packages/README.md for the overlay mechanism.
#
# Why source-built at all: the msm DPU cannot ROTATE_90 a LINEAR plane, so gamescope must rotate the
# portrait-native Pocket S2 panel in its GPU composite step (a code change → a package rebuild).
#
# Fields:
#   name           pkgname (must match the PKGBUILD); also the work/ build-dir + repo entry
#   pkgbuild_local path (relative to this dir) to the checked-in PKGBUILD to build
#   pkgrel_suffix  numeric suffix appended to the PKGBUILD's pkgrel (N -> N.<suffix>) so pacman
#                  prefers our build over holo's binary. Integer only (makepkg requires
#                  pkgrel = integer[.integer]).
#   patches        space-separated files under ./patches/, applied `patch -p1` in the gamescope
#                  source root (after `cd gamescope` in prepare()), in the order listed.
#
# To bump gamescope: edit pkgver in packages/gamescope/PKGBUILD, re-verify the patch applies against
# the new tag (patch -p1 --dry-run on a shallow clone), and re-roll it only if a hunk fails.
name: gamescope
pkgbuild_local: PKGBUILD
pkgrel_suffix: 1
patches: 0001-composite-rotation-pr2228.patch 0002-sanitize-nightmode-atom.patch 0003-drmbackend-fake-output-mm.patch 0004-fps-limit-atom-persist.patch
